
//Dark Skies DLC

TITechTemplate.displayName.BS_DemocratizationofSpace=Democratization of Space
TITechTemplate.quote.BS_DemocratizationofSpace="Even our greatest technologies only enable us to see five percent of our universe. Just imagine what we will learn once we can gaze upon the remaining ninety-five percent."<br/><align=right>{cooperateLeader}<align=left><br/><align=right>From the opening address of the annual Global Astronomers Conference.<align=left>
TITechTemplate.summary.BS_DemocratizationofSpace=Advances in aerospace technology open the skies to more people.
TITechTemplate.description.BS_DemocratizationofSpace=Low Earth orbit, filled with many thousands of new satellites, is now a testament to the changes that have been wrought by a handful of private spaceflight companies. Due to improved rocket reusability, a less risk-averse approach to research and development, and advances in satellite technology that allow them to be smaller and lighter, the cost of putting mass into orbit has dropped by more than 80 percent. This has led to an unprecedented expansion in the use of satellites in business and academia. In parallel with this, new space programs are taking shape in middle and rising powers of the world. The greater accessibility and interest in space have led to other advancements in space exploration. In particular, our ability to track nearby objects has improved considerably.

TITechTemplate.displayName.BS_ExascaleComputing=Exascale Computing
TITechTemplate.quote.BS_ExascaleComputing="Yes, knowledge is power, but power for what purpose, Ifechi? I want to believe that the more we learn, the more we grow. But the older I get, the more trouble I have shaking the feeling that we are dangerously close to the forbidden fruit of myth."<br/><align=right>{appeaseLeader}<align=left><br/><align=right>Excerpt from a letter to his partner while on assignment in Senegal.<align=left>
TITechTemplate.summary.BS_ExascaleComputing=We build systems capable of answering our most difficult scientific questions. 
TITechTemplate.description.BS_ExascaleComputing=As our datasets became ever larger and our simulations became ever more sophisticated, we needed more powerful computers to handle them. The path to this point was not linear; given the most obvious routes to improvement, the power requirements alone would have made this project infeasible. Millions of computers working together in perfect harmony, failing gracefully, and operating with unbelievable energy efficiency. But in the end, we did it, and the dividends have been immense. Advancements in protein folding and genome mapping, material science, climate modeling, engineering simulation, cosmology, and nearly every other field of scientific endeavor have brought mankind to a pinnacle of knowledge and to a precipice of technology.

TITechTemplate.displayName.BS_DigitalSociety=Digital Society
TITechTemplate.quote.BS_DigitalSociety="Bury it somewhere inside the licensing agreement. Nobody reads them, and most people don't comprehend that if they're not paying for a product, they <i>are</i> the product."<br/><align=right>{exploitLeader}<align=left><br/><align=right>Remarks during an internal product review with Freesoft Insights.</i><align=left>
TITechTemplate.summary.BS_DigitalSociety=The world becomes connected in new and potentially destabilizing ways. 
TITechTemplate.description.BS_DigitalSociety=The advent of smartphones, the mass adoption of social media, targeted advertising, bot networks, ubiquitous surveillance and sophisticated online disinformation campaigns. Any one of these could be world-changing on its own, but instead they are happening all at once, alongside countless other changes to our way of life. The age of the algorithm is here, and our problems are multiplying faster than we can find solutions. It's into this strange, chaotic world of innovation living alongside pessimism that something fundamentally new has entered. The question is whether it is yet another problem, or the long-awaited solution. 